Task: assign a STRUCTURAL role to each signal. Structural roles describe how a column behaves, not what it measures:
continuous_measured (noisy, continuously varying), actuator_like (step-like / piecewise constant, often 0-100), held_sampled (updates every k samples, analyzer-like), constant, derived_redundant (near-exact function of other signals), counter (monotone index), timestamp, categorical, text, identifier, unknown.
Use the statistics given (stuck fraction, quantization step, autocorrelation, update period, noise level, relation to other signals). Sample rows, when provided, are local-only context and are weak evidence.
